1
00:00:01,106 --> 00:00:04,026
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:06,111
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,646 --> 00:00:44,066
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:46,985
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:47,069 --> 00:00:49,071
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:52,157 --> 00:00:53,784
[♪ upbeat music playing]

7
00:01:05,837 --> 00:01:07,339
EPISODE 5

8
00:01:11,343 --> 00:01:12,552
[cell phone vibrating]

9
00:01:13,553 --> 00:01:14,554
Hmm?

10
00:01:16,807 --> 00:01:18,350
Good morning, Mr. Choi.

11
00:01:18,433 --> 00:01:20,310
Good morning.

12
00:01:20,394 --> 00:01:21,687
[Isoo] What made you call so early?

13
00:01:22,312 --> 00:01:23,980
I booked a consultation for you.

14
00:01:24,690 --> 00:01:27,776
[sighs] I told you I don't like shrinks.

15
00:01:27,859 --> 00:01:30,696
What if I get hypnotized again
and do something? I'm not going.

16
00:01:30,779 --> 00:01:32,864
I'm worried about you.

17
00:01:32,948 --> 00:01:35,158
Why do you worry so much? Huh?

18
00:01:35,242 --> 00:01:37,035
Didn't you see me catch those hitmen?

19
00:01:37,119 --> 00:01:38,537
Nothing bad happened.

20
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:40,580
Just listen to me.

21
00:01:40,664 --> 00:01:42,416
Ignoring it won't make it go away.

22
00:01:42,499 --> 00:01:44,251
You get yourself checked out first.

23
00:01:44,334 --> 00:01:46,795
Ignoring indigestion won't make it better.

24
00:01:46,878 --> 00:01:48,046
[sighs in exasperation]

25
00:01:49,423 --> 00:01:50,841
Will you go if I go?

26
00:01:51,466 --> 00:01:53,510
Of course. You go first, then I'll go.

27
00:01:53,593 --> 00:01:55,429
I have to go to work now. Bye.

28
00:01:56,012 --> 00:01:57,013
[line disconnects]

29
00:01:58,682 --> 00:01:59,891
[sighs in exasperation]

30
00:01:59,975 --> 00:02:01,101
[sets down phone]

31
00:02:01,643 --> 00:02:02,727
[inhales]

32
00:02:03,562 --> 00:02:04,771
[exhales deeply]

33
00:02:15,407 --> 00:02:16,491
[elevator dings]

34
00:02:21,288 --> 00:02:22,289
[digital beep]

35
00:02:28,003 --> 00:02:29,254
[exhales softly]

36
00:02:29,337 --> 00:02:31,256
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

37
00:02:31,339 --> 00:02:32,424
[audio distorts]

38
00:02:32,507 --> 00:02:33,759
[muffled metallic clinking]

39
00:02:33,842 --> 00:02:35,635
[high-pitched tone droning]

40
00:02:38,263 --> 00:02:39,306
[groans]

41
00:02:39,848 --> 00:02:40,849
[thud]

42
00:02:42,768 --> 00:02:44,311
[slow heartbeats]

43
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:48,023
[groans]

44
00:02:50,442 --> 00:02:52,360
-[elevator clunks]
-[grunts]

45
00:02:53,278 --> 00:02:54,905
[breathing heavily]

46
00:02:56,490 --> 00:02:57,908
[metallic clinking intensifies]

47
00:02:59,618 --> 00:03:01,244
[high-pitched ringing intensifies]

48
00:03:03,872 --> 00:03:05,248
[panting]

49
00:03:05,332 --> 00:03:06,416
[audio normalizes]

50
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:10,670
[♪ gentle, somber music playing]

51
00:03:18,804 --> 00:03:20,013
[inhales]

52
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:21,765
[elevator dings]

53
00:03:21,848 --> 00:03:23,225
[continues panting]

54
00:03:31,816 --> 00:03:32,943
[♪ music fades]

55
00:03:33,985 --> 00:03:36,821
ROSEBUD HOTEL

56
00:03:36,905 --> 00:03:38,949
-[woman] I'm so excited!
-[chuckles]

57
00:03:39,032 --> 00:03:40,367
[♪ quirky music playing]

58
00:03:40,951 --> 00:03:42,911
-Welcome.
-Hello.

59
00:03:42,994 --> 00:03:44,829
-We made a reservation.
-Yes, we did.

60
00:03:44,913 --> 00:03:46,289
May I have your name?

61
00:03:46,373 --> 00:03:47,624
Lee Gwanghui.

62
00:03:47,707 --> 00:03:49,584
-Lee Gwanghui?
-[keyboard clacking]

63
00:03:49,668 --> 00:03:52,337
-Why are you so cute today?
-Because today's a special day.

64
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:54,089
Really? Oh...

65
00:03:54,172 --> 00:03:56,716
I'm sorry, but I can't seem
to find your reservation.

66
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:58,802
What? Uh...

67
00:03:58,885 --> 00:04:00,720
Then please try "Oh Gyeonghwa."

68
00:04:00,804 --> 00:04:02,389
-Please.
-Oh Gyeonghwa.

69
00:04:02,472 --> 00:04:03,640
Even her name's pretty.

70
00:04:04,182 --> 00:04:05,183
[Gyeonghwa giggles]

71
00:04:05,267 --> 00:04:07,269
-[keyboard clacking]
-[couple chattering indistinctly]

72
00:04:08,061 --> 00:04:10,063
I'm sorry,
but I can't find your reservation.

73
00:04:11,147 --> 00:04:12,899
-What?
-What's going on, babe?

74
00:04:13,817 --> 00:04:16,486
That can't be right.
I'm sure I made a reservation. I...
STYLE
::cue()

75
00:04:17,988 --> 00:04:20,699
I think I canceled to get
a lower rate and never rebooked.

76
00:04:22,617 --> 00:04:24,327
Ah. Forget it. I'm leaving.

77
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,329
Wait, hold on.

78
00:04:26,913 --> 00:04:27,914
So...

79
00:04:29,541 --> 00:04:30,959
Could you perhaps save me?

80
00:04:31,042 --> 00:04:32,127
I mean,

81
00:04:32,919 --> 00:04:34,170
do you have any rooms left?

82
00:04:34,254 --> 00:04:35,797
On White Day? As if.

83
00:04:36,590 --> 00:04:37,591
One moment, please.

84
00:04:37,674 --> 00:04:39,885
Everyone's walking around with candy.

85
00:04:39,968 --> 00:04:41,386
I assumed mine was in the room.

86
00:04:41,469 --> 00:04:43,763
-I really hope you have a room.
-Yes, we have one.

87
00:04:43,847 --> 00:04:46,099
You do? We'll take it.

88
00:04:46,182 --> 00:04:47,601
The last room on the seventh floor.

89
00:04:47,684 --> 00:04:49,978
-Thank you. They had a room.
-Thank you.

90
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:52,272
-You're so annoying!
-Come on.

91
00:04:52,355 --> 00:04:55,483
At least make an effort.

92
00:04:57,485 --> 00:04:58,486
[clicks tongue]

93
00:04:58,570 --> 00:05:01,615
I wish you'd forget what happened earlier.

94
00:05:01,698 --> 00:05:04,117
-I can't forget it.
-Babe.

95
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,994
It's our one-year anniversary.

96
00:05:06,077 --> 00:05:07,662
I wish you would.

97
00:05:09,414 --> 00:05:10,415
I'll let it slide.

98
00:05:10,498 --> 00:05:12,334
[groans affectionately] You're so cute.

99
00:05:12,876 --> 00:05:16,755
[sighs] What am I supposed to do
if you're this cute even when you're mad?

100
00:05:16,838 --> 00:05:18,882
I can't help it. I was born this way.

101
00:05:18,965 --> 00:05:20,884
-I think I'm trapped.
-Me too.

102
00:05:20,967 --> 00:05:23,386
-Please save us!
-Save us!

103
00:05:23,470 --> 00:05:24,512
[elevator dings]

104
00:05:24,596 --> 00:05:26,222
[Gwanghui] We're saved. [chuckles]

105
00:05:27,849 --> 00:05:29,517
Wait, stop.

106
00:05:29,601 --> 00:05:31,353
We can't just go like this.

107
00:05:31,436 --> 00:05:33,229
-Here, hold this.
-Hmm?

108
00:05:33,772 --> 00:05:34,981
[clears throat, spits]

109
00:05:35,941 --> 00:05:37,067
[squeals]

110
00:05:37,984 --> 00:05:39,027
[grunts]

111
00:05:39,778 --> 00:05:41,780
-What are you doing?
-[panting]

112
00:05:41,863 --> 00:05:42,989
My knees...

113
00:05:43,073 --> 00:05:45,533
It's our anniversary today.

114
00:05:45,617 --> 00:05:48,036
So your feet won't be touching
the ground all day.

115
00:05:48,119 --> 00:05:49,120
Okay!

116
00:05:49,329 --> 00:05:50,956
[♪ quirky music playing]

117
00:05:54,876 --> 00:05:55,919
Now, where are we?

118
00:05:57,837 --> 00:06:00,090
-Am I heavy?
-[continues panting] No.

119
00:06:01,633 --> 00:06:03,009
You're light as a feather.

120
00:06:03,093 --> 00:06:05,387
You should stop losing weight.

121
00:06:05,470 --> 00:06:07,597
-You're lighter than a strand of hair.
-Okay.

122
00:06:07,681 --> 00:06:09,724
-Now, where is our room?
-Over there.

123
00:06:09,808 --> 00:06:11,309
Here we are!

124
00:06:11,893 --> 00:06:12,978
-Okay!
-Here?

125
00:06:13,061 --> 00:06:14,437
Yes, go on.

126
00:06:15,605 --> 00:06:16,648
-Go on.
-Wait.

127
00:06:16,731 --> 00:06:18,358
Hold it properly for it to...

128
00:06:18,441 --> 00:06:20,193
-Try placing it carefully.
-Okay.

129
00:06:20,276 --> 00:06:21,361
-[card reader beeps]
-It worked!

130
00:06:21,444 --> 00:06:22,529
It worked!

131
00:06:22,779 --> 00:06:23,989
-It worked!
-It worked.

132
00:06:24,072 --> 00:06:25,073
Here we go!

133
00:06:25,156 --> 00:06:26,491
-[exclaims excitedly]
-[panting]

134
00:06:26,574 --> 00:06:27,784
-It's gorgeous.
-This room is amazing.

135
00:06:28,118 --> 00:06:29,869
[shrieks] It's so beautiful!

136
00:06:29,953 --> 00:06:31,788
-It's beautiful.
-Yes, it's so beautiful.

137
00:06:32,872 --> 00:06:35,041
-[grunting]
-Isn't it great?

138
00:06:35,125 --> 00:06:36,334
[♪ ominous sting]

139
00:06:37,210 --> 00:06:38,586
-[exclaims]
-[squeals]

140
00:06:39,379 --> 00:06:41,589
Babe, you're so manly!

141
00:06:41,673 --> 00:06:43,550
Babe! Are you leaving?

142
00:06:46,761 --> 00:06:48,430
[♪ ominous sting]

143
00:06:48,513 --> 00:06:50,056
[screaming]

144
00:06:55,895 --> 00:06:58,064
[sighs] They really shouldn't have
sent me all these.

145
00:06:58,148 --> 00:06:59,190
Honestly.

146
00:07:00,108 --> 00:07:01,192
Kyungjin.

147
00:07:01,693 --> 00:07:02,694
Ooh, what's that?

148
00:07:02,777 --> 00:07:04,237
It's for White Day.

149
00:07:04,863 --> 00:07:06,573
-Thank you.
-Detective Park...

150
00:07:06,656 --> 00:07:07,741
PARK JUNYOUNG

151
00:07:09,659 --> 00:07:12,662
He took a day off on White Day?

152
00:07:13,371 --> 00:07:14,372
That's very fishy.

153
00:07:14,456 --> 00:07:15,707
What is?

154
00:07:15,790 --> 00:07:18,752
My exceptional detective instincts
are kicking in.

155
00:07:19,502 --> 00:07:23,590
That clueless Detective Park who only
listens to trot music is dating someone?

156
00:07:23,673 --> 00:07:26,134
-He said he's meeting his mom.
-Right?

157
00:07:26,968 --> 00:07:28,970
Who would date someone like him?

158
00:07:29,053 --> 00:07:30,513
I'm sure he went to see his mom.

159
00:07:30,597 --> 00:07:32,056
[♪ quirky music playing]

160
00:07:32,140 --> 00:07:33,308
Is it White Day today?

161
00:07:33,975 --> 00:07:35,101
-[Kim Suwon] Yes.
-[Byungsik exclaims]

162
00:07:35,685 --> 00:07:36,811
I forgot last year, too.

163
00:07:36,895 --> 00:07:37,896
Hey.

164
00:07:39,522 --> 00:07:41,274
-Got any cash?
-Just pay by card.

165
00:07:41,357 --> 00:07:42,567
I use my wife's card.

166
00:07:42,650 --> 00:07:44,360
[Kim Suwon] Do I look like I have money?

167
00:07:44,444 --> 00:07:45,653
Lend me 20,000 won.

168
00:07:46,905 --> 00:07:48,281
Come on, just 20,000 won.

169
00:07:48,364 --> 00:07:49,491
Just 20,000 won.

170
00:07:51,075 --> 00:07:52,285
[whispers] He's surprisingly devoted.

171
00:07:52,911 --> 00:07:54,412
[whispers] I heard
his wife is really scary.

172
00:07:54,496 --> 00:07:55,622
[gasps]

173
00:07:56,456 --> 00:07:57,874
What about you?

174
00:07:57,957 --> 00:08:00,627
[sighs] I've already got my surprise
all planned out.

175
00:08:00,710 --> 00:08:02,670
You're so diligent. A true romantic.

176
00:08:02,754 --> 00:08:04,881
-Aren't you going to date, bro?
-Hey.

177
00:08:04,964 --> 00:08:07,509
I prefer to meet people naturally.

178
00:08:07,592 --> 00:08:09,260
Look at these. That's...

179
00:08:12,055 --> 00:08:13,056
It's a new case.

180
00:08:14,182 --> 00:08:16,893
We got a report of a body. Rosebud Hotel.

181
00:08:18,978 --> 00:08:20,688
-Yes! You what?
-Today, I--

182
00:08:20,772 --> 00:08:22,690
What about White Day?
The case comes first.

183
00:08:22,774 --> 00:08:23,817
Okay, let's go.

184
00:08:24,692 --> 00:08:26,611
-[Kyungjin] Come on.
-The case should come first.

185
00:08:27,278 --> 00:08:28,613
[Kyungjin] But, bro, seriously...
STYLE
::cue()

186
00:08:32,909 --> 00:08:34,285
We're with Gangha Police.

187
00:08:34,369 --> 00:08:36,996
ROSEBUD HOTEL CONCIERGE
JEON YUJIN

188
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,081
Right.

189
00:08:38,665 --> 00:08:39,791
I'm the general manager.

190
00:08:39,874 --> 00:08:41,209
ROSEBUD HOTEL GENERAL MANAGER
YU JONGYEOL

191
00:08:41,292 --> 00:08:42,293
Hello.

192
00:08:42,377 --> 00:08:43,962
[♪ enthralling music playing]

193
00:08:46,756 --> 00:08:48,007
Where's the scene?

194
00:08:48,091 --> 00:08:49,134
In Room 709.

195
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:51,928
[chuckles]

196
00:08:52,011 --> 00:08:53,012
[gasps]

197
00:08:54,597 --> 00:08:56,307
[♪ quirky music playing]

198
00:08:56,724 --> 00:08:57,809
Detective Park.

199
00:08:59,018 --> 00:09:00,395
What are you doing here?

200
00:09:00,979 --> 00:09:01,980
I called him.

201
00:09:02,647 --> 00:09:03,940
Why? It's his day off.

202
00:09:04,023 --> 00:09:05,608
The case comes first.

203
00:09:06,651 --> 00:09:08,069
Dr. Yoon?

204
00:09:08,153 --> 00:09:09,654
Dr. Yoon from Forensic Pathology? Oh!

205
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:13,283
Gosh, Detective Jin.
Fancy meeting you here.

206
00:09:13,366 --> 00:09:14,534
[Isoo] What are you doing here?

207
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:17,287
I have plans, obviously. [chuckles]

208
00:09:17,871 --> 00:09:19,205
I was actually on my way out.

209
00:09:19,289 --> 00:09:20,665
This is perfect timing.

210
00:09:20,748 --> 00:09:22,292
-A body was found here.
-What?

211
00:09:22,375 --> 00:09:23,877
-Come with us.
-But I...

212
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:25,128
You're here.

213
00:09:26,171 --> 00:09:27,505
-[Dr. Yoon] Oh.
-Yeah.

214
00:09:27,589 --> 00:09:29,382
You were here, too. [chuckles softly]

215
00:09:29,465 --> 00:09:30,633
Hello, Dr. Yoon.

216
00:09:30,717 --> 00:09:31,718
Dr. Yoon.

217
00:09:32,427 --> 00:09:33,636
We've met before.

218
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:35,513
Oh, yes, Detective Joo.

219
00:09:35,597 --> 00:09:36,723
[chuckles]

220
00:09:36,806 --> 00:09:38,474
I look forward to working with you.

221
00:09:38,558 --> 00:09:39,684
Likewise.

222
00:09:40,602 --> 00:09:41,603
Please follow me.

223
00:09:42,478 --> 00:09:43,563
Come on, let's go.

224
00:09:43,646 --> 00:09:45,899
-Let's go.
-[clears throat] Yes, let's go.

225
00:09:48,693 --> 00:09:49,986
So Dr. Yoon is his mom?

226
00:09:50,069 --> 00:09:51,821
Did you see that? They were linking arms.

227
00:09:51,905 --> 00:09:53,740
-They jumped apart in surprise.
-[giggles]

228
00:09:53,823 --> 00:09:56,367
-What plans did they have at a hotel?
-[Kyungjin] Drumroll.

229
00:10:01,915 --> 00:10:02,916
This is the place.

230
00:10:02,999 --> 00:10:04,459
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

231
00:10:15,887 --> 00:10:17,805
It looks like she's been dead for a while.

232
00:10:18,932 --> 00:10:20,600
It's been at least 12 hours.

233
00:10:21,935 --> 00:10:23,561
It looks like she was stabbed.

234
00:10:27,023 --> 00:10:29,442
-In three places.
-Right.

235
00:10:31,402 --> 00:10:34,739
She was stabbed in three places,
but there's not much bleeding.

236
00:10:35,615 --> 00:10:36,866
[sighs]

237
00:10:36,950 --> 00:10:39,619
Bleeding can be minimal.
It depends where you were stabbed.

238
00:10:40,370 --> 00:10:42,705
-I'll check during the autopsy.
-Okay.

239
00:10:46,542 --> 00:10:47,835
Her phone.

240
00:10:56,511 --> 00:10:57,887
[Kyungjin] I don't see the murder weapon.

241
00:10:59,889 --> 00:11:01,933
-Get this to forensics.
-Yes, ma'am.

242
00:11:04,978 --> 00:11:06,854
-Hello, sir.
-Detective Joo.

243
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:11,609
We can't find the murder weapon,
and there's little blood.

244
00:11:11,693 --> 00:11:13,444
-I'll take a look.
-Okay.

245
00:11:14,779 --> 00:11:16,698
-You stay here, Detective Park.
-Got it.

246
00:11:21,953 --> 00:11:23,413
Do you know the victim?

247
00:11:24,038 --> 00:11:25,999
Her name's Oh Minyeong. She a concierge.

248
00:11:27,041 --> 00:11:28,918
Where is the person who found the body?

249
00:11:29,002 --> 00:11:30,211
They're at the bar.

250
00:11:30,795 --> 00:11:31,796
This way, please.

251
00:11:35,675 --> 00:11:37,802
-What?
-Are you even human?

252
00:11:37,885 --> 00:11:39,721
I am. I'm human.

253
00:11:39,804 --> 00:11:41,556
I'm drinking because I'm human.

254
00:11:41,639 --> 00:11:43,057
You're worse than an animal.

255
00:11:43,141 --> 00:11:45,893
Don't talk that way.
Have some manners in a place like this.

256
00:11:45,977 --> 00:11:48,604
-You're seriously saying that right now?
-Babe.

257
00:11:48,688 --> 00:11:50,523
-Hello.
-Gosh, you startled me.
STYLE
::cue()

258
00:11:55,611 --> 00:11:57,113
Aren't you Jin Isoo?

259
00:11:57,196 --> 00:11:58,740
Yes, I am.

260
00:11:58,823 --> 00:11:59,824
[shrieks excitedly]

261
00:11:59,907 --> 00:12:02,452
Oh my god. You're so good-looking.

262
00:12:02,535 --> 00:12:04,203
He's not that good-looking.

263
00:12:04,287 --> 00:12:05,413
No one asked you, ugly.

264
00:12:05,496 --> 00:12:07,165
[Gwanghui] Ugly?
You've got to be kidding me.

265
00:12:07,248 --> 00:12:08,791
Can I get a photo with you?

266
00:12:08,875 --> 00:12:10,209
-Why not?
-[Gyeonghwa] Thank you.

267
00:12:10,293 --> 00:12:11,544
-Ugly, huh?
-I'll take it.

268
00:12:11,627 --> 00:12:12,628
Thanks.

269
00:12:13,379 --> 00:12:14,630
One, two, three.

270
00:12:14,714 --> 00:12:16,049
[Gwanghui] Don't stand too close.

271
00:12:16,132 --> 00:12:17,342
-[camera shutter clicks]
-[squeals]

272
00:12:18,593 --> 00:12:20,261
Oh, uh, is she your girlfriend?

273
00:12:20,345 --> 00:12:22,180
Gosh, of course not.

274
00:12:22,263 --> 00:12:23,389
We're police.

275
00:12:23,473 --> 00:12:24,891
[Isoo] I'm here to work.

276
00:12:24,974 --> 00:12:27,060
You found the body, didn't you?

277
00:12:27,143 --> 00:12:28,895
Can you explain what happened?

278
00:12:30,730 --> 00:12:34,984
We started dating on White Day last year.

279
00:12:35,068 --> 00:12:37,487
So I made a reservation
for our one-year anniversary,

280
00:12:37,570 --> 00:12:39,864
but there was a bit of a problem.

281
00:12:39,947 --> 00:12:41,574
You were too cheap to book it.

282
00:12:41,657 --> 00:12:44,410
You're really going to humiliate me
in front of other people?

283
00:12:44,494 --> 00:12:45,620
I said it was a mistake.

284
00:12:45,703 --> 00:12:46,788
And?

285
00:12:47,372 --> 00:12:50,375
Ah, so our reservation was canceled,

286
00:12:50,458 --> 00:12:53,294
but it turns out they had one room left.

287
00:12:53,378 --> 00:12:56,214
They had a room left on White Day?

288
00:12:56,297 --> 00:12:57,673
They would've been overbooked.

289
00:12:57,757 --> 00:12:58,966
No, they had a room left.

290
00:13:00,218 --> 00:13:03,137
So I carried my adorable baby

291
00:13:03,221 --> 00:13:04,680
and walked down the hallway.

292
00:13:04,764 --> 00:13:07,517
Yes, exactly.
It was straight out of a movie. [chuckles]

293
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,143
Since we're on the subject,

294
00:13:09,227 --> 00:13:11,354
you were a little heavier
than you used to be.

295
00:13:11,437 --> 00:13:14,440
-I almost threw my back out.
-You said I was as light as a feather.

296
00:13:14,524 --> 00:13:15,817
Don't be ridiculous.

297
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:17,402
Hey, Mr. Ugly.

298
00:13:18,152 --> 00:13:19,237
Let's focus here.

299
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:21,572
-Yes, Mr. Ugly.
-Right.

300
00:13:21,656 --> 00:13:24,409
So we opened the door like this,

301
00:13:24,492 --> 00:13:26,786
but then, some woman

302
00:13:26,869 --> 00:13:29,163
was right there behind the bed,
like a ghost.

303
00:13:29,247 --> 00:13:30,915
With her eyes wide open.

304
00:13:31,999 --> 00:13:33,751
So we just ran out of there.

305
00:13:35,378 --> 00:13:38,673
Why leave out the part where
you threw me onto the bed? Embarrassed?

306
00:13:38,756 --> 00:13:41,300
[scoffs] You're bent on making me
look like a coward, aren't you?

307
00:13:41,384 --> 00:13:42,885
I told you, I was just startled.

308
00:13:42,969 --> 00:13:45,847
Exactly. You ditch your girlfriend
when you're startled.

309
00:13:45,930 --> 00:13:47,265
I just panicked for a second.

310
00:13:47,348 --> 00:13:49,142
-Enough. I'm upset.
-And I'm humiliated!

311
00:13:49,225 --> 00:13:50,351
Okay, focus.

312
00:13:51,978 --> 00:13:54,105
Did you touch anything inside the room?

313
00:13:54,188 --> 00:13:55,314
Or see anything strange?

314
00:13:56,774 --> 00:13:57,817
No.

315
00:13:57,900 --> 00:13:59,026
Nothing like that.

316
00:13:59,902 --> 00:14:01,362
Thank you for your cooperation.

317
00:14:01,445 --> 00:14:02,655
We may contact you again.

318
00:14:02,738 --> 00:14:03,739
Okay.

319
00:14:03,823 --> 00:14:05,283
[Isoo inhales sharply]

320
00:14:05,366 --> 00:14:07,493
-He looks familiar.
-[Gyeonghwa] Bye.

321
00:14:09,203 --> 00:14:10,580
You and I are over!

322
00:14:10,663 --> 00:14:12,373
How many times must I apologize?

323
00:14:12,456 --> 00:14:14,500
-Fine, blame me for being a coward.
-[Isoo sighs]

324
00:14:14,584 --> 00:14:16,377
It's like watching a soap opera.

325
00:14:16,460 --> 00:14:17,587
That's why I don't date.

326
00:14:18,713 --> 00:14:19,839
Isn't it that you can't?

327
00:14:21,924 --> 00:14:22,925
With this face?

328
00:14:24,510 --> 00:14:25,511
[scoffs]

329
00:14:26,012 --> 00:14:27,722
She's the narcissistic one.

330
00:14:28,973 --> 00:14:30,141
[whispers] She's unbelievable.

331
00:14:30,224 --> 00:14:32,768
Just go. Don't let my screaming stop you.

332
00:14:37,398 --> 00:14:39,400
We've prepared a suite for you.

333
00:14:39,483 --> 00:14:40,985
Please stay as long as you like.

334
00:14:41,068 --> 00:14:42,445
[♪ dramatic music playing]

335
00:14:44,447 --> 00:14:45,448
During your stay,

336
00:14:45,531 --> 00:14:48,910
all hotel services, including
food and beverages, are complimentary.

337
00:14:50,411 --> 00:14:52,455
-Including alcohol?
-Of course.

338
00:14:52,538 --> 00:14:53,748
[gasps]

339
00:14:53,831 --> 00:14:54,832
Get up.

340
00:14:54,916 --> 00:14:56,667
You love free stuff, babe.

341
00:14:57,251 --> 00:14:58,669
-[Gwanghui] Let's go.
-[Gyeonghwa giggles]

342
00:15:01,714 --> 00:15:02,715
[sighs]

343
00:15:02,798 --> 00:15:03,799
Jeez.

344
00:15:04,550 --> 00:15:05,551
[scoffs]

345
00:15:05,635 --> 00:15:07,220
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

346
00:15:07,970 --> 00:15:10,556
I don't think I saw her
after 7:00 p.m. last night.

347
00:15:10,640 --> 00:15:11,641
Right?

348
00:15:12,308 --> 00:15:13,351
Yes, that's right.

349
00:15:15,895 --> 00:15:20,066
Do you know anyone who might've had
a grudge against Ms. Oh Minyeong?
STYLE
::cue()

350
00:15:23,319 --> 00:15:25,112
I'm not sure.

351
00:15:25,196 --> 00:15:29,367
Did she have any trouble
with any guests at all?

352
00:15:31,827 --> 00:15:32,954
[chuckles nervously]

353
00:15:34,413 --> 00:15:35,414
[clears throat]

354
00:15:37,667 --> 00:15:41,254
The hotel was all red and glossy,
but why is the back of house like this?

355
00:15:41,837 --> 00:15:44,966
What about the staff?
They have rights too, don't they?

356
00:15:45,049 --> 00:15:46,050
Wait.

357
00:15:47,343 --> 00:15:49,428
-I'll be right back.
-Where are you going?

358
00:15:49,512 --> 00:15:51,138
To canvass the area.

359
00:15:54,267 --> 00:15:57,061
HOUSEKEEPING

360
00:15:57,144 --> 00:15:58,229
[knocking]

361
00:15:58,312 --> 00:16:00,314
-[housekeeper 1] Yes?
-Excuse me.

362
00:16:00,398 --> 00:16:01,440
[♪ quirky music playing]

363
00:16:01,524 --> 00:16:02,692
-Goodness.
-He's handsome.

364
00:16:02,775 --> 00:16:05,403
-Aren't you the heir of Hansu Group?
-You're right.

365
00:16:05,486 --> 00:16:06,737
Oh...

366
00:16:06,821 --> 00:16:08,739
You ladies have a sharp eye.

367
00:16:08,823 --> 00:16:10,574
Hear that? He called me a lady.

368
00:16:10,658 --> 00:16:12,576
-It was me.
-No, it was me, silly.

369
00:16:13,411 --> 00:16:16,414
What's a chaebol heir doing
all the way down here?

370
00:16:16,497 --> 00:16:19,917
I'm in charge of Ms. Oh Minyeong's case.

371
00:16:20,001 --> 00:16:22,461
-Ah...
-"In charge of"?

372
00:16:22,545 --> 00:16:23,796
He's a detective.

373
00:16:23,879 --> 00:16:25,881
He rammed a helicopter
into a car last year.

374
00:16:25,965 --> 00:16:27,883
Yes, that was me.

375
00:16:27,967 --> 00:16:30,469
-[chuckles] I think I saw that, too.
-[housekeeper 1] Right?

376
00:16:30,553 --> 00:16:31,721
Excuse me.

377
00:16:31,804 --> 00:16:34,140
Did Minyeong really die?

378
00:16:35,266 --> 00:16:39,020
Yes, so I was wondering if I could get
some help from you lovely ladies.

379
00:16:39,103 --> 00:16:42,648
Gosh, you keep calling us ladies
and flattering us like that.

380
00:16:43,232 --> 00:16:45,192
Ow! You're pretty strong.

381
00:16:45,276 --> 00:16:47,987
Try working here for three months,
you'll bulk right up.

382
00:16:48,070 --> 00:16:49,905
We're all wearing matching outfits.

383
00:16:49,989 --> 00:16:51,615
-You're right.
-Me too.

384
00:16:52,450 --> 00:16:54,076
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

385
00:17:05,796 --> 00:17:07,173
Detective Joo.

386
00:17:07,256 --> 00:17:09,216
This is Ms. Oh Minyeong's shift log.

387
00:17:09,300 --> 00:17:10,926
You should take a look at this.

388
00:17:11,010 --> 00:17:12,011
[housekeeper 1] Minyeong?

389
00:17:12,094 --> 00:17:14,430
Men just wouldn't leave her alone.

390
00:17:14,513 --> 00:17:16,349
She's gorgeous.

391
00:17:16,432 --> 00:17:19,518
Being pretty isn't easy. I would know.

392
00:17:19,602 --> 00:17:21,479
I was quite the catch back in the day.

393
00:17:21,562 --> 00:17:23,647
-You're still beautiful.
-[scoffs playfully]

394
00:17:23,731 --> 00:17:27,318
Honestly, you have good taste.
[chuckles]

395
00:17:27,985 --> 00:17:30,780
I think some of the staff
asked her out as well.

396
00:17:30,863 --> 00:17:31,864
-[housekeeper 1] Really?
-Yeah.

397
00:17:32,406 --> 00:17:34,200
Have you seen anyone suspicious lately?

398
00:17:34,909 --> 00:17:36,619
-Anyone suspicious?
-Were there any?

399
00:17:37,536 --> 00:17:38,579
[murmuring quietly]

400
00:17:39,246 --> 00:17:40,289
Ah!

401
00:17:40,373 --> 00:17:41,707
-Room 701.
-The ugly guy?

402
00:17:41,791 --> 00:17:43,084
-Yes.
-Room 701?

403
00:17:43,167 --> 00:17:46,587
I heard he's a chaebol heir.
He's been in the suite for three weeks.

404
00:17:46,671 --> 00:17:47,838
And?

405
00:17:48,547 --> 00:17:50,633
He kept calling for Minyeong,

406
00:17:50,716 --> 00:17:52,176
saying he had requests to make.

407
00:17:52,259 --> 00:17:53,260
[housekeeper 2] That's right.

408
00:17:53,969 --> 00:17:56,806
He stared at her in this creepy way
and followed her around.

409
00:17:56,889 --> 00:17:57,890
Right.

410
00:17:57,973 --> 00:17:59,058
That funny-looking man.

411
00:17:59,141 --> 00:18:00,768
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

412
00:18:00,851 --> 00:18:02,269
Funny-looking?

413
00:18:03,854 --> 00:18:05,648
He called for her multiple times a day.

414
00:18:05,731 --> 00:18:07,191
REMARKS
ATTENDED TO ROOM 701

415
00:18:07,274 --> 00:18:09,443
Who is the guest in Room 701?

416
00:18:10,653 --> 00:18:12,988
That guest is confidential,
so I can't say.

417
00:18:14,031 --> 00:18:15,908
Do you have cameras on the seventh floor?

418
00:18:18,577 --> 00:18:20,121
The camera on the seventh floor

419
00:18:20,955 --> 00:18:22,957
-is off.
-Why?

420
00:18:24,083 --> 00:18:26,877
It broke down two months ago,
but it hasn't been repaired yet.

421
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:31,257
A five-star hotel just left
a broken security camera?

422
00:18:31,799 --> 00:18:33,551
That doesn't make sense to me.

423
00:18:35,761 --> 00:18:36,887
[Jongyeol] Uh...

424
00:18:37,513 --> 00:18:39,849
A maintenance report wasn't filed.
It was a mistake.

425
00:18:43,352 --> 00:18:44,478
[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

426
00:18:45,062 --> 00:18:47,815
You two meet with Ms. Oh's family
and break the news.

427
00:18:48,524 --> 00:18:49,775
See what they have to say.

428
00:18:49,859 --> 00:18:51,277
-Got it. Let's go.
-Got it.

429
00:18:56,031 --> 00:18:57,533
[line connects, ringing]

430
00:18:59,744 --> 00:19:01,245
[cell phone vibrating]

431
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:03,914
[♪ gritty blues-rock music playing]

432
00:19:03,998 --> 00:19:05,624
SHADOW WITHOUT A TRACE
TRACK TO THE END

433
00:19:05,708 --> 00:19:07,042
JEONG MINJAE DETECTIVE AGENCY

434
00:19:07,126 --> 00:19:08,753
HYERA

435
00:19:08,836 --> 00:19:10,463
[cell phone continues vibrating]

436
00:19:13,090 --> 00:19:14,300
Hey, it's been a while.

437
00:19:14,383 --> 00:19:16,719
Yeah. How's the business going?

438
00:19:16,802 --> 00:19:19,555
It looks like word got around.
I've been swamped.

439
00:19:20,181 --> 00:19:21,807
[chuckles] I have a favor to ask.

440
00:19:21,891 --> 00:19:22,975
What is it?

441
00:19:23,058 --> 00:19:24,477
Rosebud Hotel.

442
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:28,147
It's a murder case, but the security
camera on the seventh floor is down.

443
00:19:28,230 --> 00:19:31,650
I need you to use the backdoor
to find out when and how it went offline.

444
00:19:31,734 --> 00:19:33,569
I told you I'm busy.

445
00:19:33,652 --> 00:19:35,488
It'll take you 10 minutes.

446
00:19:35,988 --> 00:19:36,989
Five minutes.

447
00:19:37,656 --> 00:19:38,908
-Gopchang?
-Deal.

448
00:19:38,991 --> 00:19:40,618
-I'll call you later.
-Okay.

449
00:19:40,993 --> 00:19:42,661
-[line disconnects]
-[hurried footsteps approaching]

450
00:19:42,745 --> 00:19:44,371
-[Isoo] Detective Joo!
-Yeah.

451
00:19:44,455 --> 00:19:45,456
[in English] Big news!

452
00:19:46,290 --> 00:19:48,167
-[in Korean] Did you learn something?
-Of course.

453
00:19:48,250 --> 00:19:50,252
There's a suspect
in the seventh-floor suite.

454
00:19:50,336 --> 00:19:52,755
Yeah, he kept calling for Ms. Oh.
Let's go meet him.

455
00:19:52,838 --> 00:19:54,048
Let's go.

456
00:20:06,101 --> 00:20:07,478
Chunsik?

457
00:20:07,561 --> 00:20:08,604
Oh.

458
00:20:09,730 --> 00:20:10,731
Isoo!

459
00:20:10,815 --> 00:20:13,150
KANG CHUNSIK
SOLE HEIR OF CHUNSIK FOOD

460
00:20:14,151 --> 00:20:15,820
-"Isoo"?
-[Isoo] Yeah.

461
00:20:16,362 --> 00:20:18,697
This is Kang Chunsik,
the sole heir of Chunsik Food.

462
00:20:19,281 --> 00:20:20,282
[softly] Oh.

463
00:20:20,366 --> 00:20:22,117
[♪ gripping, dramatic music playing]

464
00:20:22,201 --> 00:20:24,620
He looks old,
but he's two years younger than us.

465
00:20:24,703 --> 00:20:26,038
He was born in 1994.

466
00:20:26,121 --> 00:20:28,624
What a nice thing to say
first thing in the morning.

467
00:20:28,707 --> 00:20:30,084
Morning, huh?

468
00:20:30,167 --> 00:20:31,585
It's 5:00 p.m. Anyway, go inside.

469
00:20:31,669 --> 00:20:33,003
-Why?
-Come inside.

470
00:20:33,087 --> 00:20:34,088
What's going on?

471
00:20:37,883 --> 00:20:39,385
[Isoo] Whoa...

472
00:20:39,468 --> 00:20:41,720
Look at the state of this room.

473
00:20:43,430 --> 00:20:45,307
THE PERSON I FELL FOR
AT FIRST SIGHT IS...

474
00:20:45,391 --> 00:20:46,934
[Chunsik] Something sad
happened yesterday.

475
00:20:47,977 --> 00:20:48,978
[Isoo] Something sad?

476
00:20:49,061 --> 00:20:50,521
What was it? Tell me.

477
00:20:54,233 --> 00:20:55,526
What do you know about love?

478
00:20:56,485 --> 00:20:57,486
Forget it.

479
00:20:57,570 --> 00:20:58,571
[scoffs]

480
00:20:59,113 --> 00:21:01,740
You've been here three weeks.
Did you run away from home?

481
00:21:01,824 --> 00:21:02,950
No, I just...

482
00:21:03,033 --> 00:21:04,660
I just came.

483
00:21:04,743 --> 00:21:07,037
Is it because of Ms. Oh Minyeong?

484
00:21:09,373 --> 00:21:12,084
Why are you asking about Ms. Oh Minyeong?

485
00:21:12,167 --> 00:21:14,378
Her shift log says
you kept calling for her.

486
00:21:16,547 --> 00:21:17,673
Oh...

487
00:21:18,591 --> 00:21:21,343
I had requests to make, but why...

488
00:21:23,679 --> 00:21:24,847
Wait, who are you?

489
00:21:24,930 --> 00:21:28,601
She's a detective.
Be straight with us. I'm a detective, too.

490
00:21:29,685 --> 00:21:31,312
I didn't do anything wrong.

491
00:21:32,313 --> 00:21:34,523
Then why did you keep calling for her?

492
00:21:34,607 --> 00:21:36,066
Were you stalking her?

493
00:21:36,150 --> 00:21:38,444
Stalking? What are you talking about?

494
00:21:38,527 --> 00:21:39,862
[angrily] I wasn't!

495
00:21:44,241 --> 00:21:45,367
[sighs softly]

496
00:21:45,951 --> 00:21:47,328
I fell for her at first sight.

497
00:21:52,249 --> 00:21:53,876
[♪ gentle jazz music playing]

498
00:21:56,712 --> 00:21:59,131
Here is the vase you requested.

499
00:22:09,808 --> 00:22:11,226
Do you need anything else?

500
00:22:21,570 --> 00:22:22,571
[♪ music fades]

501
00:22:22,655 --> 00:22:25,991
That's what people call stalking.

502
00:22:26,075 --> 00:22:28,202
And your face already screams "suspect."

503
00:22:28,285 --> 00:22:29,954
I'm not bad-looking.

504
00:22:30,788 --> 00:22:32,206
Right?

505
00:22:32,706 --> 00:22:33,749
Uh...

506
00:22:33,832 --> 00:22:35,042
No comment.

507
00:22:35,125 --> 00:22:37,002
[Isoo] Don't you look in the mirror?

508
00:22:37,086 --> 00:22:40,589
I told you to work on your looks
if you want to date. Just look at you.

509
00:22:40,673 --> 00:22:44,051
I am working on my looks.
Do you know how expensive my clinic is?

510
00:22:44,134 --> 00:22:47,221
Excuse me, please tell us
what happened yesterday.

511
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:50,641
Yesterday...

512
00:22:54,061 --> 00:22:55,938
I asked her out.

513
00:22:56,897 --> 00:23:00,985
I couldn't hide my feelings anymore.

514
00:23:02,319 --> 00:23:03,821
If she said yes,

515
00:23:03,904 --> 00:23:05,364
today would be our anniversary.

516
00:23:07,241 --> 00:23:09,034
We'd be a White Day couple.

517
00:23:10,661 --> 00:23:11,954
[mumbles]

518
00:23:12,037 --> 00:23:13,414
With that?

519
00:23:13,497 --> 00:23:16,667
Hey, that's from that movie.
It was a whole thing 20 years ago.

520
00:23:17,376 --> 00:23:18,544
[Chunsik] Come on.

521
00:23:18,627 --> 00:23:20,838
I had the perfect plan.

522
00:23:22,172 --> 00:23:24,967
I want to confess my feelings
to the person I love.
STYLE
::cue()

523
00:23:25,551 --> 00:23:28,012
[chuckles] How can I help with that?

524
00:23:28,595 --> 00:23:29,888
Uh...

525
00:23:29,972 --> 00:23:31,932
I need flowers, balloons, and a cake.

526
00:23:32,016 --> 00:23:34,518
What kind of cake would you like?

527
00:23:34,601 --> 00:23:35,602
I'm not sure.

528
00:23:35,978 --> 00:23:37,521
Um...

529
00:23:37,604 --> 00:23:40,441
What flavor do you like, Ms. Oh?

530
00:23:42,026 --> 00:23:45,446
I'm clueless about what women like.
[chuckles]

531
00:23:46,572 --> 00:23:48,490
Our hotel is famous
for our chocolate cake.

532
00:23:49,408 --> 00:23:50,951
Then please prepare that.

533
00:23:51,035 --> 00:23:52,036
Of course.

534
00:23:52,119 --> 00:23:53,871
[♪ gentle, pleasant music playing]

535
00:24:13,098 --> 00:24:14,892
[inaudible conversation]

536
00:24:31,617 --> 00:24:33,452
Then I'll take my leave now.

537
00:24:33,535 --> 00:24:34,578
Hold on.

538
00:24:35,204 --> 00:24:38,082
I need to rehearse.

539
00:24:38,165 --> 00:24:40,959
Could you sit here for a moment?

540
00:24:41,627 --> 00:24:42,836
Just for one minute.

541
00:24:43,587 --> 00:24:44,588
[♪ music fades]

542
00:24:44,671 --> 00:24:45,714
[chuckles softly]

543
00:24:45,798 --> 00:24:47,174
Please, this way.

544
00:24:52,012 --> 00:24:53,347
Please sit here.

545
00:24:53,430 --> 00:24:54,431
Okay.

546
00:25:06,443 --> 00:25:08,237
[♪ dreamy retro music playing]

547
00:25:11,782 --> 00:25:12,783
[sharp exhale]

548
00:25:14,868 --> 00:25:16,245
I HAVE FALLEN IN LOVE

549
00:25:16,328 --> 00:25:18,080
I have fallen in love.

550
00:25:20,874 --> 00:25:22,417
I've never felt this way before.

551
00:25:23,460 --> 00:25:24,920
I'm feeling a little shy.

552
00:25:33,428 --> 00:25:35,430
She came to me with the scent of flowers.

553
00:25:36,807 --> 00:25:39,059
You must be wondering who she is.
[chuckles]

554
00:25:43,814 --> 00:25:45,983
The person I fell for at first sight is...

555
00:25:50,195 --> 00:25:51,947
It's you, Minyeong.

556
00:25:54,533 --> 00:25:56,076
Minyeong.

557
00:25:56,160 --> 00:25:57,786
I'm sorry. I have a boyfriend.

558
00:26:00,455 --> 00:26:02,249
Minyeong...

559
00:26:02,332 --> 00:26:03,625
-[♪ music fades]
-[door opens]

560
00:26:03,709 --> 00:26:05,419
[♪ soft melancholy music playing]

561
00:26:06,378 --> 00:26:07,754
Another one, please.

562
00:26:15,012 --> 00:26:16,305
[sobbing]

563
00:26:18,348 --> 00:26:19,641
One more.

564
00:26:19,725 --> 00:26:20,726
[♪ music fades]

565
00:26:23,645 --> 00:26:24,646
Just like that,

566
00:26:25,981 --> 00:26:28,108
the love of my life left me.

567
00:26:29,735 --> 00:26:31,904
What time did you call
Ms. Oh Minyeong here?

568
00:26:31,987 --> 00:26:32,988
[♪ soft suspenseful music playing]

569
00:26:33,071 --> 00:26:34,072
Around

570
00:26:34,990 --> 00:26:36,158
seven o'clock?

571
00:26:37,242 --> 00:26:38,493
What time did she leave?

572
00:26:38,577 --> 00:26:39,578
About

573
00:26:40,662 --> 00:26:42,080
Forty minutes later.

574
00:26:43,624 --> 00:26:45,792
Did she report me?

575
00:26:46,668 --> 00:26:50,088
I really didn't stalk her.
My feelings are sincere.

576
00:26:52,049 --> 00:26:53,258
[sighs deeply]

577
00:26:53,800 --> 00:26:56,637
Ms. Oh Minyeong has died.

578
00:26:56,720 --> 00:26:57,971
What?

579
00:26:58,055 --> 00:27:00,807
She was murdered last night.

580
00:27:04,728 --> 00:27:06,271
Chunsik.

581
00:27:07,022 --> 00:27:08,023
Mr. Kang.

582
00:27:08,106 --> 00:27:10,108
-[Isoo] Chunsik.
-Wake up, Mr. Kang.

583
00:27:10,192 --> 00:27:12,527
Mr. Kang, wake up.

584
00:27:12,611 --> 00:27:13,737
[Isoo] Hey, hey...

585
00:27:14,404 --> 00:27:15,489
[Hyera sighs]

586
00:27:16,949 --> 00:27:17,950
[sniffs]

587
00:27:18,450 --> 00:27:19,534
This is alcohol.

588
00:27:20,369 --> 00:27:21,662
-So it is.
-Isoo.

589
00:27:22,287 --> 00:27:25,290
[coughs] You're lying, right?

590
00:27:25,374 --> 00:27:26,959
Please tell me it's a lie.

591
00:27:27,793 --> 00:27:28,794
It's a lie, right?

592
00:27:29,920 --> 00:27:31,880
Come on, Detective.

593
00:27:32,506 --> 00:27:34,508
What in the world is going on?

594
00:27:34,591 --> 00:27:36,468
You're a detective, Isoo!

595
00:27:37,052 --> 00:27:38,553
[sobbing]

596
00:27:40,263 --> 00:27:41,640
Minyeong!

597
00:27:52,442 --> 00:27:53,819
[sighs softly]

598
00:27:53,902 --> 00:27:55,487
[Chunsik continues sobbing]

599
00:27:56,238 --> 00:27:57,322
Stop crying!
STYLE
::cue()

600
00:28:00,993 --> 00:28:03,620
Did Ms. Oh Minyeong have a boyfriend?

601
00:28:03,704 --> 00:28:04,830
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

602
00:28:04,913 --> 00:28:06,081
Uh...

603
00:28:06,164 --> 00:28:07,666
I'm not sure.

604
00:28:11,128 --> 00:28:12,170
I don't know either.

605
00:28:14,339 --> 00:28:17,342
Did anyone stay in Room 709 last night?

606
00:28:17,426 --> 00:28:20,429
No, Room 709 was unoccupied.

607
00:28:21,096 --> 00:28:22,222
It was unoccupied?

608
00:28:22,889 --> 00:28:25,183
Why did she go
to an unoccupied room alone?

609
00:28:25,267 --> 00:28:26,810
[♪ music swells, fades]

610
00:28:30,480 --> 00:28:32,107
[sobbing, ragged breathing]
Why did our daughter...

611
00:28:32,649 --> 00:28:34,484
Why did she die?

612
00:28:34,568 --> 00:28:36,319
[♪ melancholy music playing]

613
00:28:38,989 --> 00:28:40,198
[Minyeong's dad] Who did this?

614
00:28:41,742 --> 00:28:43,452
We're still investigating the matter.

615
00:28:43,535 --> 00:28:45,370
[continues sobbing, breathing raggedly]

616
00:28:48,457 --> 00:28:50,417
Did your daughter

617
00:28:51,001 --> 00:28:52,878
have a boyfriend?

618
00:28:55,589 --> 00:28:57,758
It did seem like
she was seeing someone lately.

619
00:28:57,841 --> 00:28:59,634
She even received an expensive handbag.

620
00:29:00,260 --> 00:29:02,304
I think it was one of the hotel staff.

621
00:29:02,387 --> 00:29:04,973
Did her boyfriend kill her?

622
00:29:05,057 --> 00:29:06,224
We don't know yet.

623
00:29:07,893 --> 00:29:08,894
By any chance,

624
00:29:09,603 --> 00:29:11,146
was there anyone

625
00:29:11,229 --> 00:29:13,231
who might've had a grudge against her?

626
00:29:13,315 --> 00:29:15,025
Our daughter was the sweetest girl!

627
00:29:15,108 --> 00:29:16,777
There isn't anyone like that!

628
00:29:21,073 --> 00:29:24,826
Can we take a look around her room?

629
00:29:24,910 --> 00:29:26,620
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

630
00:29:42,135 --> 00:29:43,845
[♪ music increases in tempo]

631
00:29:53,396 --> 00:29:55,107
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

632
00:29:56,191 --> 00:29:57,818
This has to be worth a fortune.

633
00:30:04,950 --> 00:30:06,326
Oh.

634
00:30:06,409 --> 00:30:07,619
This is a limited edition.

635
00:30:16,294 --> 00:30:17,671
You can't buy this with money.

636
00:30:21,675 --> 00:30:23,051
[♪ music swells, fades]

637
00:30:23,885 --> 00:30:26,638
SEWON HOSPITAL

638
00:30:34,646 --> 00:30:36,565
The name is Choi Jeonghun.

639
00:30:36,648 --> 00:30:38,400
[receptionist] Please wait just a moment.

640
00:30:50,787 --> 00:30:52,581
[♪ gentle melancholy music playing]

641
00:30:58,420 --> 00:31:00,213
[monitor beeping steadily]

642
00:31:11,183 --> 00:31:12,434
[♪ music fades]

643
00:31:16,313 --> 00:31:17,314
[clears throat softly]

644
00:31:19,649 --> 00:31:20,775
-Mr. Choi Jeonghun?
-Yes.

645
00:31:20,859 --> 00:31:22,819
-You're all done with your tests.
-Okay.

646
00:31:22,903 --> 00:31:26,114
We sent your biopsy for analysis,
so the results will take a few days.

647
00:31:26,740 --> 00:31:28,366
Let's get you booked in.

648
00:31:28,450 --> 00:31:29,492
All right.

649
00:31:29,576 --> 00:31:31,536
These two dates are available.

650
00:31:33,872 --> 00:31:35,749
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

651
00:31:43,882 --> 00:31:44,966
ROOM 709

652
00:31:45,050 --> 00:31:47,677
[Hyera] She went into
an unoccupied room and died.

653
00:31:49,346 --> 00:31:50,347
Why?

654
00:31:54,226 --> 00:31:55,727
[cell phone vibrating]

655
00:31:59,564 --> 00:32:00,565
Hey.

656
00:32:00,649 --> 00:32:02,442
That camera on the seventh floor

657
00:32:02,525 --> 00:32:04,277
isn't broken. It was turned off.
STYLE
::cue()

658
00:32:04,361 --> 00:32:06,404
It was blocked by the central server.

659
00:32:07,072 --> 00:32:08,698
January 14, at 8:00 p.m.

660
00:32:08,782 --> 00:32:09,866
MANUAL RECORDING STOP

661
00:32:09,950 --> 00:32:11,701
Okay, thank you.

662
00:32:15,205 --> 00:32:19,542
Someone manipulated the camera
and planned this murder?

663
00:32:21,086 --> 00:32:22,420
REPORTING PARTY

664
00:32:22,504 --> 00:32:23,838
LEE GWANGHUI
OH GYEONGHWA

665
00:32:25,507 --> 00:32:26,508
VICTIM, ROOM 701 GUEST

666
00:32:26,591 --> 00:32:28,802
OH MINYEONG, AGE 31
KANG CHUNSIK, AGE 30

667
00:32:28,885 --> 00:32:30,553
It had to be someone on the inside.

668
00:32:33,473 --> 00:32:36,017
Detective Joo.
Here's the crime scene report.

669
00:32:36,810 --> 00:32:39,271
This is just the fingerprints
and trace evidence.

670
00:32:39,354 --> 00:32:42,440
-We'll go over the bloodstains tomorrow.
-Okay. Thank you.

671
00:32:43,066 --> 00:32:44,067
Aren't you going home?

672
00:32:44,150 --> 00:32:46,027
I will in a bit. You go on home.

673
00:32:46,111 --> 00:32:47,570
-Okay, bye.
-Bye.

674
00:32:56,496 --> 00:32:57,497
[♪ music fades]

675
00:32:57,580 --> 00:33:01,209
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

676
00:33:07,674 --> 00:33:10,427
Someone's a real workaholic, aren't they?

677
00:33:10,510 --> 00:33:11,886
[yawning]

678
00:33:12,804 --> 00:33:14,681
-What time is it?
-It's 9:00 a.m.

679
00:33:15,265 --> 00:33:17,726
-At least sleep at home.
-[sighs]

680
00:33:19,227 --> 00:33:21,313
-The report came out?
-Yeah.

681
00:33:26,776 --> 00:33:28,778
No trace of Chunsik's fingerprints.

682
00:33:29,404 --> 00:33:30,697
Chunsik's out.

683
00:33:31,323 --> 00:33:34,576
We don't know that. They wiped the handle.

684
00:33:34,659 --> 00:33:36,661
Go wash up before you come closer.

685
00:33:39,622 --> 00:33:41,374
Hydrogen peroxide was on her clothes.

686
00:33:41,458 --> 00:33:43,251
VICTIM'S CLOTHING
HYDROGEN PEROXIDE DETECTED

687
00:33:43,335 --> 00:33:44,794
[♪ tense suspenseful music playing]

688
00:33:46,463 --> 00:33:48,840
They also found reddish-brown fibers.

689
00:33:56,681 --> 00:33:58,183
[♪ music increases in tempo]

690
00:34:04,481 --> 00:34:05,482
[♪ music fades]

691
00:34:10,653 --> 00:34:12,155
[Dr. Yoon] Light over here, please.

692
00:34:15,116 --> 00:34:16,785
[♪ soft suspenseful music playing]

693
00:34:20,455 --> 00:34:21,664
[cell phone vibrating]

694
00:34:21,748 --> 00:34:22,749
Who is it?

695
00:34:25,293 --> 00:34:27,003
It's Detective Joo Hyera.

696
00:34:27,087 --> 00:34:28,505
[Dr. Yoon] Put her on.

697
00:34:29,631 --> 00:34:30,632
DETECTIVE JOO HYERA

698
00:34:30,715 --> 00:34:31,800
[on speakerphone] Hello? Dr. Yoon?

699
00:34:31,883 --> 00:34:33,301
Have you started the autopsy?

700
00:34:33,385 --> 00:34:35,053
Yes, just now.

701
00:34:35,136 --> 00:34:37,138
Do we have an estimated time of death yet?

702
00:34:37,222 --> 00:34:39,724
Between 8:00 and 9:00 p.m.

703
00:34:39,808 --> 00:34:40,809
And the murder weapon?

704
00:34:40,892 --> 00:34:41,893
Uh...

705
00:34:42,519 --> 00:34:43,853
It's a knife,

706
00:34:44,813 --> 00:34:46,815
but not a kitchen knife.
The blade's thinner.

707
00:34:51,152 --> 00:34:53,863
The blade is about 16 mm wide.

708
00:34:56,825 --> 00:34:58,159
It has a serrated edge.

709
00:35:09,379 --> 00:35:11,005
[sobbing]

710
00:35:18,805 --> 00:35:21,725
He's still going around like that?
What's with his clothes?

711
00:35:22,934 --> 00:35:25,353
Is it true love?

712
00:35:26,646 --> 00:35:28,732
Or the crocodile tears of a killer?

713
00:35:33,486 --> 00:35:35,321
Hey, why are you buying so much bread?

714
00:35:35,405 --> 00:35:36,865
It's a tasty bribe.

715
00:35:36,948 --> 00:35:38,825
I've got my informants everywhere.

716
00:35:38,908 --> 00:35:39,909
Informants?

717
00:35:40,535 --> 00:35:41,911
Can you go pick up the coffee?

718
00:35:41,995 --> 00:35:43,371
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

719
00:35:55,008 --> 00:35:56,009
We'll take this, too.

720
00:35:56,092 --> 00:35:58,136
[bakery clerk] Yes,
I'll get it ready for you.

721
00:35:58,219 --> 00:36:00,346
Their chocolate cake is famous, remember?

722
00:36:01,222 --> 00:36:02,223
Really?
STYLE
::cue()

723
00:36:05,101 --> 00:36:06,227
[♪ music fades]

724
00:36:06,311 --> 00:36:07,437
Who are your informants?

725
00:36:08,313 --> 00:36:10,315
The people who are
invisible to the guests,

726
00:36:10,398 --> 00:36:13,693
but know everything that happens here.

727
00:36:13,777 --> 00:36:16,988
You know you can't pay people
for information, right?

728
00:36:17,071 --> 00:36:19,491
You think I'm an idiot?

729
00:36:19,574 --> 00:36:20,825
Just follow me. [clicks tongue]

730
00:36:22,827 --> 00:36:24,078
-[housekeeper 1 sighs]
-[knock at door]

731
00:36:24,162 --> 00:36:25,163
Yes.

732
00:36:26,831 --> 00:36:29,083
-I'm back.
-Goodness!

733
00:36:29,167 --> 00:36:30,710
Oh my, you're here again.

734
00:36:31,377 --> 00:36:33,379
-[housekeeper 2] What's all this?
-[housekeeper 1] Why did you buy so much?

735
00:36:33,463 --> 00:36:35,757
I bought them in case you were hungry.

736
00:36:35,840 --> 00:36:36,841
-One second.
-Goodness.

737
00:36:36,925 --> 00:36:37,926
[housekeeper 3] What is all this?

738
00:36:38,551 --> 00:36:40,929
Just leave it. We'll take care of this.

739
00:36:41,012 --> 00:36:42,013
Hey, hey.

740
00:36:42,096 --> 00:36:45,183
Don't even lift a finger.
Please take a seat.

741
00:36:45,266 --> 00:36:46,726
-[housekeeper 1] Oh my.
-Don't lift our fingers?

742
00:36:46,810 --> 00:36:47,977
[all chuckling]

743
00:36:48,061 --> 00:36:50,855
-Even my husband isn't this kind.
-What a treat.

744
00:36:50,939 --> 00:36:52,148
We're being spoiled.

745
00:36:52,732 --> 00:36:54,108
[housekeeper 3] Coffee, too?

746
00:36:54,192 --> 00:36:55,527
By the way, who is this?

747
00:36:56,110 --> 00:36:58,196
Ah. She's my team leader.

748
00:36:58,279 --> 00:36:59,531
Hello.

749
00:36:59,614 --> 00:37:01,449
-Hello.
-Hello.

750
00:37:01,533 --> 00:37:03,409
Here's your coffee.

751
00:37:03,493 --> 00:37:04,911
-Take your coffee.
-Thank you.

752
00:37:04,994 --> 00:37:06,746
[Isoo] All right, please enjoy.

753
00:37:07,247 --> 00:37:09,916
-[housekeeper 4] Thank you.
-This is my first time trying this.

754
00:37:10,667 --> 00:37:12,043
But it's from the bakery here.

755
00:37:12,126 --> 00:37:14,045
It's super expensive.

756
00:37:17,465 --> 00:37:18,591
Hmm?

757
00:37:19,509 --> 00:37:20,510
This is insane.

758
00:37:21,553 --> 00:37:22,762
It's so good.

759
00:37:22,846 --> 00:37:24,097
[all chuckle]

760
00:37:24,848 --> 00:37:26,224
It's really delicious.

761
00:37:26,307 --> 00:37:28,351
Now I see why it's 100,000 won.

762
00:37:28,434 --> 00:37:29,769
You should have some, too.

763
00:37:29,853 --> 00:37:31,813
-Yes, have some.
-[Hyera chuckles]

764
00:37:32,230 --> 00:37:34,774
All right. If you insist, I won't say no.

765
00:37:34,858 --> 00:37:36,693
-[housekeeper 1] Go on, eat up.
-[women chuckle]

766
00:37:38,528 --> 00:37:39,696
Mmm. Mmm.

767
00:37:40,572 --> 00:37:42,240
-It's delicious.
-It is, isn't it?

768
00:37:42,323 --> 00:37:43,908
[women chuckling]

769
00:37:45,118 --> 00:37:47,287
Uh, so, did you look into it?

770
00:37:47,370 --> 00:37:50,081
We gathered all the information,

771
00:37:50,164 --> 00:37:51,165
just like you said.

772
00:37:51,249 --> 00:37:52,458
Go on, tell him.

773
00:37:53,960 --> 00:37:55,461
I heard this from security.

774
00:37:56,921 --> 00:37:58,715
He was on his way to work on Wednesday.

775
00:37:58,798 --> 00:38:02,302
-[distant scuffle]
-[woman] I saw everything, you bitch!

776
00:38:02,385 --> 00:38:04,596
You've got it all wrong. It's not me!

777
00:38:04,679 --> 00:38:06,639
You psycho bitch!

778
00:38:06,723 --> 00:38:07,724
[♪ tense music playing]

779
00:38:07,807 --> 00:38:09,767
Hey, are you saying

780
00:38:09,851 --> 00:38:11,728
I'm delusional?

781
00:38:11,811 --> 00:38:13,062
You crazy...

782
00:38:13,146 --> 00:38:14,689
-Please calm down, ma'am.
-What?

783
00:38:14,772 --> 00:38:16,232
Let go!

784
00:38:16,316 --> 00:38:17,942
Are you out of your damn minds?

785
00:38:18,026 --> 00:38:19,611
Hey, do your job properly!

786
00:38:20,236 --> 00:38:21,696
Who do you think you are?

787
00:38:21,779 --> 00:38:23,990
Do you have any idea
who you're dealing with?

788
00:38:24,073 --> 00:38:26,117
Wake the hell up! Hey, get on your knees.

789
00:38:26,200 --> 00:38:27,660
I said, kneel down.

790
00:38:27,744 --> 00:38:29,913
You crazy bitch! Kneel!

791
00:38:29,996 --> 00:38:31,539
Who was she?

792
00:38:31,623 --> 00:38:32,624
It was...

793
00:38:34,667 --> 00:38:35,793
the hotel owner's wife.

794
00:38:35,877 --> 00:38:36,878
Wait,

795
00:38:37,879 --> 00:38:41,466
the owner was dating Ms. Oh Minyeong?

796
00:38:41,549 --> 00:38:43,051
No, it's not that.

797
00:38:43,134 --> 00:38:46,137
There were rumors
that he was in love with her.

798
00:38:46,220 --> 00:38:49,182
I saw him following her around as well.

799
00:38:50,725 --> 00:38:52,810
[hotel owner] Wait,
we're not done talking.

800
00:38:54,562 --> 00:38:55,813
I have nothing else to say.

801
00:38:55,897 --> 00:38:57,774
I said we're not done.

802
00:38:57,857 --> 00:38:58,858
Let go.

803
00:38:59,400 --> 00:39:00,443
[soft thud]

804
00:39:07,575 --> 00:39:08,868
We'll talk later.

805
00:39:09,869 --> 00:39:11,120
[♪ music swells, fades]
STYLE
::cue()

806
00:39:15,458 --> 00:39:17,335
He tried to drag her into Room 709?

807
00:39:18,169 --> 00:39:20,338
Yes, it was really scary.

808
00:39:21,047 --> 00:39:23,675
I've never seen the boss like that before.

809
00:39:23,758 --> 00:39:25,259
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

810
00:39:25,343 --> 00:39:28,805
Come to think of it,
there's something strange about Room 709.

811
00:39:28,888 --> 00:39:29,889
What do you mean?

812
00:39:29,973 --> 00:39:32,058
Uh, about once a week,

813
00:39:32,141 --> 00:39:34,602
we're asked to clean that room at dawn.

814
00:39:41,567 --> 00:39:42,902
But when I looked into it,

815
00:39:44,112 --> 00:39:46,280
that room has been vacant for two months.

816
00:39:46,364 --> 00:39:48,157
-[gasps]
-What on earth?

817
00:39:48,241 --> 00:39:49,701
[housekeeper 3] That's scary.

818
00:39:51,035 --> 00:39:52,203
[Hyera sighs softly]

819
00:39:52,704 --> 00:39:54,288
[no audio on footage]

820
00:39:58,876 --> 00:40:01,254
[door opens, closes]

821
00:40:02,714 --> 00:40:04,132
What's going on?

822
00:40:06,217 --> 00:40:08,845
There was an assault here last Wednesday.

823
00:40:08,928 --> 00:40:11,639
Shouldn't you have told us
something like this had happened?

824
00:40:12,598 --> 00:40:14,100
I didn't think it was relevant.

825
00:40:14,183 --> 00:40:16,019
Not relevant?

826
00:40:16,102 --> 00:40:18,187
It looks like she wants to kill Ms. Oh.

827
00:40:18,771 --> 00:40:21,399
She looks pretty strong, too.
She's our first suspect.

828
00:40:21,482 --> 00:40:22,483
I doubt it.

829
00:40:23,317 --> 00:40:24,902
She won't have killed her.

830
00:40:25,945 --> 00:40:27,196
Why don't we check?

831
00:40:28,156 --> 00:40:29,949
What's her license plate number?

832
00:40:30,616 --> 00:40:32,076
[surveillance operator] It's 0948.

833
00:40:32,160 --> 00:40:35,413
Can I see the parking garage entry log
from the day of the murder?

834
00:40:37,874 --> 00:40:39,042
Here you go.

835
00:40:46,049 --> 00:40:48,259
She came in at 7:42 p.m.

836
00:40:48,843 --> 00:40:51,888
Please show me
where she went after 7:42 p.m.

837
00:40:51,971 --> 00:40:53,973
[♪ gripping suspenseful music continues]

838
00:41:03,149 --> 00:41:04,275
[scoffs]

839
00:41:05,401 --> 00:41:07,487
She even disguised herself.

840
00:41:08,237 --> 00:41:10,740
I heard the hotel owner
was chasing after Ms. Oh.

841
00:41:11,532 --> 00:41:13,034
There were rumors about that,

842
00:41:13,701 --> 00:41:14,911
but I don't know anything.

843
00:41:16,037 --> 00:41:18,081
Why was Room 709 left vacant?

844
00:41:18,790 --> 00:41:20,958
I heard it was left
unoccupied for two months.

845
00:41:24,462 --> 00:41:28,549
Oddly enough, it coincides with the time
the seventh-floor camera was broken.

846
00:41:28,633 --> 00:41:29,634
Two months.

847
00:41:30,343 --> 00:41:32,595
No, the camera wasn't broken.

848
00:41:36,641 --> 00:41:39,644
The central server stopped recording.

849
00:41:43,147 --> 00:41:44,732
Are you going to keep interfering?

850
00:41:46,526 --> 00:41:48,152
Explain what happened.

851
00:41:48,319 --> 00:41:50,113
[♪ music swells, fades]

852
00:41:56,661 --> 00:41:58,162
I was following the CEO's orders.

853
00:41:58,246 --> 00:42:00,039
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

854
00:42:00,123 --> 00:42:01,624
The CEO's orders?

855
00:42:01,707 --> 00:42:02,708
Yes.

856
00:42:04,001 --> 00:42:07,839
He told me to turn off the security camera
and leave Room 709 unoccupied.

857
00:42:07,922 --> 00:42:08,923
For what reason?

858
00:42:10,341 --> 00:42:11,509
I really don't know.

859
00:42:12,593 --> 00:42:13,678
Where is he right now?

860
00:42:15,555 --> 00:42:16,806
He has a prior commitment,

861
00:42:18,099 --> 00:42:19,517
so he'll be in this afternoon.

862
00:42:19,600 --> 00:42:20,810
[♪ music swells]

863
00:42:23,688 --> 00:42:24,772
[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

864
00:42:24,856 --> 00:42:27,483
The hotel owner also stalked
Ms. Oh Minyeong?

865
00:42:28,943 --> 00:42:31,320
His wife suspected
they were having an affair

866
00:42:31,404 --> 00:42:32,905
and assaulted Ms. Oh Minyeong.

867
00:42:32,989 --> 00:42:36,325
On the day of the murder, his wife
and daughter came here in disguise.

868
00:42:36,409 --> 00:42:37,451
[scoffs]

869
00:42:37,535 --> 00:42:39,787
What on earth is going on?

870
00:42:40,788 --> 00:42:43,332
Room 709 was left vacant for two months.

871
00:42:43,416 --> 00:42:45,084
On the owner's orders.

872
00:42:45,168 --> 00:42:48,880
The owner, Yeom Jaeseop, left more
prints at the scene than anyone else.

873
00:42:48,963 --> 00:42:50,715
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

874
00:42:50,798 --> 00:42:53,217
YEOM JAESEOP'S FINGERPRINTS
DETECTED MOST FREQUENTLY

875
00:42:53,301 --> 00:42:57,513
What was he doing with the security camera
off and that room left vacant?

876
00:42:57,597 --> 00:42:59,140
[clicks tongue, inhales deeply]

877
00:42:59,223 --> 00:43:01,517
He's coming in the afternoon,
so you two find out.

878
00:43:01,601 --> 00:43:03,769
-We'll go meet his wife.
-Got it.

879
00:43:03,853 --> 00:43:06,564
Don't push him too hard.
Just see what he says.

880
00:43:06,647 --> 00:43:07,940
Understood.

881
00:43:08,024 --> 00:43:09,483
[engine roaring]

882
00:43:10,735 --> 00:43:12,195
[engine downshifts, brakes squeal]

883
00:43:13,070 --> 00:43:14,113
[ignition clicks off]

884
00:43:22,955 --> 00:43:24,624
[gate bell chimes]

885
00:43:28,753 --> 00:43:30,796
I'm Joo Hyera, with Gangha Police.

886
00:43:33,174 --> 00:43:35,343
You must've seen
the dermatologist this morning.

887
00:43:35,426 --> 00:43:36,427
[sighs]

888
00:43:36,510 --> 00:43:37,511
WIFE OF YEOM JAESEOP
CHA SERAN

889
00:43:37,595 --> 00:43:39,180
I can't take these off yet.

890
00:43:40,598 --> 00:43:42,350
What's this about?

891
00:43:42,433 --> 00:43:44,977
What else could it be?
That bitch must've reported us.

892
00:43:45,061 --> 00:43:46,896
Are you talking about Ms. Oh Minyeong?

893
00:43:46,979 --> 00:43:49,232
She can sue me if she wants.
I'll do the same.

894
00:43:50,149 --> 00:43:51,400
That shameless bitch.

895
00:43:51,484 --> 00:43:53,194
[sighs] What's got you so upset?

896
00:43:53,277 --> 00:43:55,071
[sighs] Don't even get me started.

897
00:43:55,655 --> 00:43:57,907
Just thinking about it
makes my blood boil.

898
00:43:59,575 --> 00:44:01,619
I should've just killed her back then.

899
00:44:01,702 --> 00:44:03,162
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

900
00:44:10,962 --> 00:44:12,380
We're with Gangha Police.

901
00:44:13,005 --> 00:44:14,548
Is the CEO inside?

902
00:44:19,345 --> 00:44:21,555
OWNER OF ROSEBUD HOTEL
YEOM JAESEOP

903
00:44:23,307 --> 00:44:25,518
Are you aware that Ms. Oh Minyeong died?

904
00:44:27,186 --> 00:44:28,354
Yes, I heard.

905
00:44:28,437 --> 00:44:30,856
She was murdered in Room 709.

906
00:44:33,276 --> 00:44:34,527
[Seran] I have this friend.

907
00:44:34,610 --> 00:44:36,570
She runs a luxury boutique.

908
00:44:37,488 --> 00:44:41,075
She said my husband asked her
to find him a limited-edition handbag.

909
00:44:41,158 --> 00:44:44,161
I assumed it was a gift for me and waited.

910
00:44:46,998 --> 00:44:47,999
Look at this.

911
00:44:50,793 --> 00:44:53,421
[scoffs] He gave it to that bitch.

912
00:44:53,504 --> 00:44:55,756
How could I not lose it after seeing that?

913
00:44:56,799 --> 00:44:57,967
How did you take these?

914
00:44:58,050 --> 00:45:00,136
He's been acting strange
for a few months now.

915
00:45:00,845 --> 00:45:03,723
He couldn't stop smiling
and had his head in the clouds.

916
00:45:04,890 --> 00:45:07,810
I figured he was seeing another woman
and had him followed.

917
00:45:08,894 --> 00:45:12,273
His office is visible
from the building next to the hotel.

918
00:45:13,065 --> 00:45:14,817
Is she going to sue me?

919
00:45:14,900 --> 00:45:16,402
After doing this behind my back?

920
00:45:17,528 --> 00:45:18,738
That evil bitch.

921
00:45:21,741 --> 00:45:22,867
Ms. Oh Minyeong

922
00:45:23,826 --> 00:45:24,952
is deceased.

923
00:45:25,036 --> 00:45:26,370
What?

924
00:45:29,582 --> 00:45:31,625
She was murdered
at the hotel two nights ago.

925
00:45:35,504 --> 00:45:36,589
In Room 709?

926
00:45:37,465 --> 00:45:38,466
Yes.

927
00:45:38,549 --> 00:45:41,802
We heard you instructed the staff
to keep that room vacant.

928
00:45:41,886 --> 00:45:42,928
Yes.

929
00:45:45,389 --> 00:45:48,309
I kept that room for my own personal use.

930
00:45:48,392 --> 00:45:50,394
Your personal use?

931
00:45:50,478 --> 00:45:53,439
We're getting ready to open
a new hotel in Gangbuk.

932
00:45:53,522 --> 00:45:55,941
I had a lot of work,
so I often stayed the night here.

933
00:45:56,025 --> 00:45:58,611
So I kept a room aside for my own use.

934
00:45:59,445 --> 00:46:02,490
But it's peak season soon,
so I told them to reopen it on the 14th.

935
00:46:03,115 --> 00:46:06,202
Why would Ms. Oh Minyeong
have died in that room?

936
00:46:08,621 --> 00:46:09,872
I wouldn't know.

937
00:46:11,499 --> 00:46:15,878
There are rumors
that you had feelings for her.

938
00:46:17,713 --> 00:46:19,882
You even bought her a designer handbag.

939
00:46:19,965 --> 00:46:21,092
[sighs defeatedly]

940
00:46:23,803 --> 00:46:26,180
Yes, well, I suppose I did.

941
00:46:27,890 --> 00:46:29,683
But I didn't do anything to her.

942
00:46:30,476 --> 00:46:31,894
I swear.

943
00:46:33,771 --> 00:46:36,273
At 7:42 p.m. that day,

944
00:46:36,357 --> 00:46:37,817
you two came to the hotel.

945
00:46:39,860 --> 00:46:42,446
Here, look. With your faces covered,
acting suspiciously.

946
00:46:42,530 --> 00:46:43,864
It's all on camera.

947
00:46:45,491 --> 00:46:48,411
Wait, are you saying
STYLE
::cue()

948
00:46:49,245 --> 00:46:50,871
that we killed that bitch?

949
00:46:50,955 --> 00:46:53,707
-It wasn't us.
-Why did you go to the hotel?

950
00:46:56,794 --> 00:46:59,046
Are you aware
that your wife assaulted Ms. Oh?

951
00:47:00,297 --> 00:47:02,925
My wife misunderstood.
She's pathologically jealous.

952
00:47:03,551 --> 00:47:05,469
Ms. Oh must've been really angry.

953
00:47:06,637 --> 00:47:09,807
Yes, so I agreed to transfer her
to the new hotel as a manager.

954
00:47:09,890 --> 00:47:11,976
[scoffs, inhales deeply]

955
00:47:12,059 --> 00:47:13,227
Of all places,

956
00:47:13,310 --> 00:47:16,564
a murder happened in Room 709,
the one you used personally,

957
00:47:16,647 --> 00:47:17,982
and of all times,

958
00:47:18,065 --> 00:47:20,151
the camera on the seventh floor is down,

959
00:47:20,234 --> 00:47:22,027
so we can't seem to identify a suspect.

960
00:47:24,780 --> 00:47:26,449
The security camera is down?

961
00:47:29,410 --> 00:47:30,828
I didn't know that.

962
00:47:38,502 --> 00:47:41,714
"I'll kill Oh Minyeong and go to hell."

963
00:47:42,423 --> 00:47:44,300
-That's what you thought, no?
-No.

964
00:47:44,383 --> 00:47:47,303
We were only
trying to catch them in the act.

965
00:47:47,386 --> 00:47:48,721
Kill her?

966
00:47:48,804 --> 00:47:51,682
-What a horrible thing to say.
-[phone clatters on table]

967
00:47:52,516 --> 00:47:54,768
-Then why did you go there?
-Well,

968
00:47:55,394 --> 00:47:56,645
my husband

969
00:47:57,229 --> 00:48:00,941
swore up and down that it wasn't true
and promised he'd start coming home early.

970
00:48:02,443 --> 00:48:06,113
But that afternoon, he didn't answer
his phone or come home.

971
00:48:06,864 --> 00:48:10,117
They were together again
because it was White Day.

972
00:48:10,951 --> 00:48:12,870
[exhales deeply] White Day, again.

973
00:48:12,953 --> 00:48:14,955
I'm starting to hate White Day.

974
00:48:15,581 --> 00:48:16,665
So?

975
00:48:17,333 --> 00:48:18,584
[♪ foreboding music playing]

976
00:48:18,667 --> 00:48:19,960
[Seran] I went to his office,

977
00:48:21,879 --> 00:48:22,880
but he wasn't there.

978
00:48:22,963 --> 00:48:25,132
-Where did he go?
-Let's go, Mom.

979
00:48:25,799 --> 00:48:27,259
That man, I swear.

980
00:48:28,219 --> 00:48:31,305
So I went to the security office
and searched through the footage.

981
00:48:40,773 --> 00:48:42,191
Where is he going?

982
00:48:42,274 --> 00:48:43,567
And I saw him

983
00:48:43,651 --> 00:48:45,361
go down to the seventh floor.

984
00:48:46,946 --> 00:48:48,155
At what time?

985
00:48:50,366 --> 00:48:52,618
[scoffs] Are you kidding me?

986
00:48:52,701 --> 00:48:55,913
Around 7:50 p.m.?

987
00:48:55,996 --> 00:48:57,623
Yeah, it was 7:50 p.m.

988
00:48:57,706 --> 00:49:00,459
[Seran] Right. We missed him by a hair.

989
00:49:01,126 --> 00:49:04,922
So I rang every doorbell.

990
00:49:05,005 --> 00:49:06,549
[doorbells ringing]

991
00:49:07,633 --> 00:49:09,426
-Where is he hiding?
-Where are they?

992
00:49:11,387 --> 00:49:12,471
Come out here!

993
00:49:14,265 --> 00:49:15,891
Where are you? [exclaims]

994
00:49:15,975 --> 00:49:18,269
-Dad!
-Come out.

995
00:49:18,352 --> 00:49:19,353
Right now!

996
00:49:20,062 --> 00:49:21,981
I went back to the security office,

997
00:49:22,064 --> 00:49:23,607
and he was on the 10th floor.

998
00:49:24,316 --> 00:49:25,651
So I went there...

999
00:49:26,610 --> 00:49:28,195
[sighs] ...and he was there.

1000
00:49:28,279 --> 00:49:29,613
What time was that?

1001
00:49:29,697 --> 00:49:31,365
It was 8...

1002
00:49:31,448 --> 00:49:33,659
Around 8:20 p.m.

1003
00:49:33,742 --> 00:49:36,745
[sharp inhale]
You'll get into trouble if you lie to us.

1004
00:49:36,829 --> 00:49:39,164
I'm not lying.
The front desk clerk was there, too.

1005
00:49:39,248 --> 00:49:40,374
Yes, you're right.

1006
00:49:40,457 --> 00:49:41,667
That good-looking kid.

1007
00:49:41,750 --> 00:49:43,377
[Jaeseop] Then you leave!

1008
00:49:44,295 --> 00:49:45,421
Jaeseop.

1009
00:49:54,680 --> 00:49:57,308
[angrily] Where were you? [exclaims]

1010
00:49:57,975 --> 00:49:59,226
He was being scolded.

1011
00:50:02,813 --> 00:50:04,356
I'm telling the truth!

1012
00:50:05,232 --> 00:50:08,068
[scoffs incredulously]
How could I possibly kill someone?

1013
00:50:08,152 --> 00:50:09,278
God, seriously...

1014
00:50:09,987 --> 00:50:11,989
It wasn't me. I didn't kill her.

1015
00:50:12,573 --> 00:50:13,741
I didn't!

1016
00:50:13,824 --> 00:50:15,784
Then why did you disguise yourself?

1017
00:50:15,868 --> 00:50:16,994
Uh...

1018
00:50:17,077 --> 00:50:20,497
How could I show up there
after the scene I made last week?

1019
00:50:20,581 --> 00:50:21,665
I have to save face.

1020
00:50:22,249 --> 00:50:23,542
[Isoo scoffs]

1021
00:50:23,626 --> 00:50:26,170
You grabbed her by the hair,
but you want to save face?

1022
00:50:26,253 --> 00:50:27,671
You'll see when you're married.

1023
00:50:27,755 --> 00:50:30,591
It's not easy keeping an eye on
such a successful husband. [sighs]

1024
00:50:30,674 --> 00:50:33,761
CEO MINDSET
DESIGNING THE VALUE OF STAYS

1025
00:50:35,471 --> 00:50:37,306
Detective Park? Still at the hotel?

1026
00:50:37,389 --> 00:50:38,849
[Junyoung] Yes.

1027
00:50:38,932 --> 00:50:42,770
At 8:20 p.m., Mr. Yeom was supposedly
with the front desk clerk in his office.

1028
00:50:43,437 --> 00:50:45,439
-Verify that for me.
-Okay, got it.

1029
00:50:46,273 --> 00:50:50,319
At around 8:20 p.m. on the 13th,
did you go to the CEO's office?

1030
00:50:51,445 --> 00:50:53,739
Yes. He wanted to see me.

1031
00:50:54,698 --> 00:50:55,991
Why do you ask?

1032
00:50:56,075 --> 00:50:58,118
[chuckles]
We're just verifying statements.

1033
00:50:58,702 --> 00:51:01,413
Did you see the CEO's wife
and his daughter there?

1034
00:51:01,497 --> 00:51:03,999
Yes. They came in together.
STYLE
::cue()

1035
00:51:07,252 --> 00:51:09,797
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

1036
00:51:09,880 --> 00:51:11,423
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

1037
00:51:12,007 --> 00:51:13,634
MARRIED
SUSPECTS AFFAIR

1038
00:51:15,427 --> 00:51:17,805
8:00 P.M.,
ESTIMATED TIME OF DEATH, 9:00 P.M.

1039
00:51:24,603 --> 00:51:27,481
[sharp inhale] I've got this feeling
Yeom Jaeseop is our guy.

1040
00:51:28,273 --> 00:51:29,817
He does seem suspicious.

1041
00:51:29,900 --> 00:51:31,402
And his statement doesn't add up.

1042
00:51:31,485 --> 00:51:34,905
He killed an employee he stalked
inside his own hotel?

1043
00:51:34,988 --> 00:51:36,949
In the room he used, no less?

1044
00:51:37,032 --> 00:51:38,325
Maybe it doesn't make sense.

1045
00:51:39,910 --> 00:51:41,161
What about his wife?

1046
00:51:42,204 --> 00:51:43,247
She was paranoid.

1047
00:51:43,330 --> 00:51:46,333
She would've heard about
the broken camera at the security office.

1048
00:51:46,917 --> 00:51:49,128
Who would kill someone
they assaulted a week ago?

1049
00:51:49,211 --> 00:51:50,337
Unless they're an idiot.

1050
00:51:51,088 --> 00:51:53,382
Nothing seems to add up, huh?

1051
00:51:53,465 --> 00:51:56,385
[sharp inhale] There's no motive,

1052
00:51:56,468 --> 00:51:57,803
and no murder weapon.

1053
00:51:57,886 --> 00:51:59,054
Detective Joo.

1054
00:52:01,348 --> 00:52:03,267
-You said the bloodstains were small.
-[Hyera] Yes.

1055
00:52:03,350 --> 00:52:05,644
[forensics officer] We took the carpet in
for testing,

1056
00:52:05,728 --> 00:52:07,187
and there wasn't enough blood.

1057
00:52:08,021 --> 00:52:10,274
We checked thoroughly,
but found no blood spatter.

1058
00:52:10,983 --> 00:52:13,152
I don't think she was murdered here.

1059
00:52:13,235 --> 00:52:15,070
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

1060
00:52:18,741 --> 00:52:20,033
She died somewhere else?

1061
00:52:20,117 --> 00:52:22,077
Did the culprit move the body?

1062
00:52:22,161 --> 00:52:24,204
Huh? That's so creepy.

1063
00:52:24,288 --> 00:52:27,541
Then they wiped the blood
with hydrogen peroxide.

1064
00:52:27,624 --> 00:52:28,667
HYDROGEN PEROXIDE DETECTED

1065
00:52:30,169 --> 00:52:31,462
[sighs deeply]

1066
00:52:31,545 --> 00:52:33,464
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

1067
00:52:35,591 --> 00:52:37,050
[line ringing over car audio]

1068
00:52:38,385 --> 00:52:40,512
-Ma'am, I have a favor to ask.
-[housekeeper] Okay.

1069
00:52:40,596 --> 00:52:43,056
Ms. Oh was murdered somewhere else.

1070
00:52:43,140 --> 00:52:46,143
Please find out if anyone saw
anything unusual while cleaning.

1071
00:52:46,226 --> 00:52:47,478
Okay, got it.

1072
00:52:48,395 --> 00:52:49,813
[line disconnects]

1073
00:52:51,774 --> 00:52:53,192
[engine roaring]

1074
00:52:55,402 --> 00:52:57,112
Oh my goodness. [breathing heavily]

1075
00:53:00,240 --> 00:53:02,242
-[radio beeps]
-This is your manager.

1076
00:53:02,326 --> 00:53:05,704
We have an urgent request
from Detective Jin Isoo.

1077
00:53:05,788 --> 00:53:07,623
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

1078
00:53:09,541 --> 00:53:11,543
-[remote beeps]
-[motorized curtains whirring]

1079
00:53:39,112 --> 00:53:40,864
Are you checking out?

1080
00:53:42,699 --> 00:53:44,034
[keyboard clacking]

1081
00:53:46,745 --> 00:53:48,038
[sighs softly]

1082
00:53:49,790 --> 00:53:50,791
[remote beeps]

1083
00:54:08,517 --> 00:54:10,018
What's this?

1084
00:54:11,186 --> 00:54:12,187
[sniffs]

1085
00:54:16,066 --> 00:54:17,734
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1086
00:54:29,621 --> 00:54:30,706
[clerk] Your payment's all set.

1087
00:54:32,499 --> 00:54:34,626
Your car is waiting outside.

1088
00:54:48,265 --> 00:54:49,850
[♪ music swells]

1089
00:54:52,603 --> 00:54:53,604
[♪ music fades]

1090
00:54:58,900 --> 00:54:59,901
SECRET AGENT DELTA

1091
00:55:01,778 --> 00:55:04,364
-[digital beep]
-Yes, Ms. Delta.

1092
00:55:05,449 --> 00:55:07,242
[♪ ominous music playing]

1093
00:55:07,326 --> 00:55:09,703
Detective Jin, it's Room 701.

1094
00:55:09,786 --> 00:55:10,871
Room 701?

1095
00:55:11,788 --> 00:55:13,081
What about Room 701?

1096
00:55:13,165 --> 00:55:14,374
[Ms. Delta] I came in to clean,

1097
00:55:15,667 --> 00:55:17,628
and I found something
that looks like blood.

1098
00:55:17,711 --> 00:55:18,962
What?

1099
00:55:19,046 --> 00:55:21,006
[♪ tense suspenseful music playing]

1100
00:55:23,675 --> 00:55:25,510
[flesh squelching]

1101
00:55:28,555 --> 00:55:29,765
[blood splatters]

1102
00:55:35,520 --> 00:55:36,772
Kang Chunsik.

1103
00:55:39,316 --> 00:55:40,984
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1104
00:55:42,611 --> 00:55:43,779
[swears softly]

1105
00:55:44,488 --> 00:55:45,947
[engine roaring, tires screech]
STYLE
::cue()

1106
00:55:57,876 --> 00:55:59,127
[Hyera] Watch out!

1107
00:55:59,211 --> 00:56:01,755
Don't worry. My car's more expensive.

1108
00:56:03,006 --> 00:56:05,676
[scoffs] How dare he try to take me on?

1109
00:56:06,927 --> 00:56:07,969
[grunts softly]

1110
00:56:08,720 --> 00:56:09,971
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

1111
00:56:10,055 --> 00:56:11,473
-[siren blaring]
-[Isoo exclaims smugly]

1112
00:56:19,231 --> 00:56:20,273
[tires screech]

1113
00:56:22,192 --> 00:56:23,360
[engine roaring]

1114
00:56:34,079 --> 00:56:35,080
Hey, hey.

1115
00:56:35,163 --> 00:56:36,998
Vehicle ahead, stop the car.

1116
00:56:37,791 --> 00:56:40,293
The trust-fund kid in car 6383!

1117
00:56:40,377 --> 00:56:41,920
Stop the car!

1118
00:56:44,005 --> 00:56:45,632
Stop the car!

1119
00:56:47,509 --> 00:56:48,677
[tires screech]

1120
00:56:54,891 --> 00:56:56,059
My good citizens!

1121
00:56:56,143 --> 00:56:58,145
Chunsik Food's sole heir is on the run!

1122
00:56:58,854 --> 00:57:01,273
We are police.

1123
00:57:01,356 --> 00:57:03,984
Kang Chunsik is on the run!

1124
00:57:04,651 --> 00:57:06,570
Kang Chunsik, stop the damn car!

1125
00:57:06,653 --> 00:57:07,779
[sighs defeatedly]

1126
00:57:08,864 --> 00:57:10,073
[tires screeching]

1127
00:57:10,157 --> 00:57:11,366
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

1128
00:57:11,450 --> 00:57:13,994
That brat just won't listen.

1129
00:57:15,287 --> 00:57:16,371
Here we go.

1130
00:57:16,455 --> 00:57:18,123
-[engine revs]
-[tires screeching]

1131
00:57:18,206 --> 00:57:19,875
[siren continues blaring]

1132
00:57:19,958 --> 00:57:20,959
[tires screech]

1133
00:57:34,973 --> 00:57:36,683
[tires screeching]

1134
00:57:51,072 --> 00:57:52,491
[engine revving]

1135
00:57:54,743 --> 00:57:55,786
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 5

1136
00:57:55,869 --> 00:57:57,579
DO THE BLOODSTAINS POINT
TO KANG CHUNSIK?

1137
00:57:57,662 --> 00:57:59,664
[♪ upbeat pop music playing,
Hersh "Shadows In The Night"]

1138
00:58:22,187 --> 00:58:25,607
Special Cast.
Special Cast. Choi Dukmoon, Lee Suk

1139
00:58:25,690 --> 00:58:29,110
Special Cast.
Ko Gunhan, Seo Hyewon

1140
00:58:32,697 --> 00:58:33,698
Look who's busted.

1141
00:58:33,782 --> 00:58:35,992
-Minyeong died in my hotel room?
-[thud]

1142
00:58:36,076 --> 00:58:37,994
[sobbing] Do you have any idea
how much I loved her?

1143
00:58:38,453 --> 00:58:39,913
If that was an act, she deserves an Oscar.

1144
00:58:39,996 --> 00:58:41,164
Are you going to keep lying?

1145
00:58:41,248 --> 00:58:43,124
There's only an eight-minute gap.

1146
00:58:43,208 --> 00:58:45,502
-That's impossible, isn't it?
-It's impossible without an accomplice.

1147
00:58:45,585 --> 00:58:47,671
-[Kyungjin] Yeom Jaeseop left the country!
-You have a private jet.

1148
00:58:47,754 --> 00:58:49,840
Captain! We're off to Hanoi!

1149
00:58:49,923 --> 00:58:51,675
Jin Isoo is here!

1150
00:58:51,758 --> 00:58:53,093
Did you kill her? [exclaims]

1151
00:58:53,176 --> 00:58:54,302
[Isoo] Come on, seriously?

1152
00:58:54,386 --> 00:58:56,096
We met secretly in Room 709.

1153
00:58:56,555 --> 00:58:58,306
-Let's end this.
-Stop what?

1154
00:58:58,390 --> 00:58:59,891
She was definitely alive
when I left the room.

1155
00:58:59,975 --> 00:59:02,060
Someone was trying to frame me.

1156
00:59:07,983 --> 00:59:09,734
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1157
00:59:19,202 --> 00:59:20,912
-Mr. Hwang.
-[both chuckling]

1158
00:59:20,996 --> 00:59:22,747
Young master. You're here.

1159
00:59:22,831 --> 00:59:24,791
You've gotten old.

1160
00:59:25,292 --> 00:59:27,252
-Did you clean the place?
-Yes, of course.

1161
00:59:28,962 --> 00:59:30,422
Go on inside.

1162
00:59:40,765 --> 00:59:42,559
[♪ ominous music playing]

1163
01:00:10,086 --> 01:00:11,421
[exhales softly]

1164
01:00:13,548 --> 01:00:15,967
[♪ melancholy piano music playing
over record player]

1165
01:00:43,662 --> 01:00:45,664
Translated by Hyesoo Lee

